    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0757" n="659" xml:id="pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5034 China—Searchlight Publishing Co./30:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-08-08T16:00:00-04:00">August 8, 1932—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>236. Your 361, August 4, 1 p.m., paragraph 3, first sentence stating that
                    “Searchlight Publishing Company have never been registered in the Consulate
                    General”.</p>
                <p>Your despatch No. 8090 of January 22 to Department<anchor n="21" xml:id="d734-f1"
                    /> transmits for Department’s consideration copy of an application made by
                    Isaacs for registration of the Searchlight Publishing Company. Department’s
                    instruction in reply to March 28<anchor n="21" xml:id="d734-f2"/> stated that
                    the Department “does not desire to raise any objection to the approval by you of
                    the application for registration”. Please inform Department what transpired
                    thereafter in connection with the application.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
